      "slug": "gen-gaussian-elimination-002",
      "solution": "$R_2 \\leftarrow R_2 - 2R_1$ gives $y - z = -1$. $R_3 \\leftarrow R_3 - 2R_1$ gives $-y = -2$, so $y = 2$.\nThen $z = y + 1 = 3$ and $x = 6 - 2 - 3 = 1$. Check: $2x + 3y + z = 2 + 6 + 3 = 11$.\n",
      "source_url": null,
      "stem": "Solve the system $x + y + z = 6$, $2x + 3y + z = 11$, $2x + y + 2z = 10$ by Gaussian elimination.\nWhat is the value of $z$?\n",
